## Package comparison

The Phase 5 package remains aligned with the approved plan. It stays within singleton startup, listener-first server ownership, bounded Effect scheduling, and terminal skew handling.

## Findings

### Critical — Production listener-first shutdown still deadlocks on blocked coordinator work

`packages/music-core/session/server.ts:665-724` still awaits connection children before closing the selected coordinator scope. Connection forwarding can wait for a blocked coordinator worker, while that worker is interrupted only by the later `closeCoordinator`. The blocked-sampling fixture still bypasses the selected post-bind graph, so the green suite does not exercise this production cancellation cycle. Redesign the ownership scopes and run the regression through the real selected graph.

### High — Marker acquisition remains interruptible before its lease is recorded

The exported Effect boundary and typed-error preservation address two prior findings, but `packages/music-core/session/client.ts:770-778` calls `restore(...)` around `acquireStartupMarkerLease`. That acquisition Promise does not consume an abort signal. If the fiber is interrupted while it is pending, Effect can stop awaiting it and skip the following `Ref.set`, while the underlying filesystem Promise can still complete exclusive acquisition and leave a marker with no recorded lease for the finalizer. Keep the non-cancellable acquisition and lease recording in one uninterruptible region, then honor interruption after the lease is registered and releasable.

### High — Startup timing and release-error policy remain incomplete

`startupSchedule` still uses a fixed 25 ms uncapped exponential policy and only `startupAttempts`; there are no validated initial/max timing settings through the tagged config boundary. `client.ts:805-813` also ignores marker-release failure, so the secondary failure is neither retained nor reported. Add bounded/capped validated timing and preserve the primary outcome together with release diagnostics as required.

### High — Startup failures are still not schema-tagged

`MusicSessionStartupError` remains a plain `Error` class (`client.ts:596-605`), although the package requires a schema-tagged startup/launch error with stable operation, message, and cause. The workflow now preserves existing `Error` instances correctly, but its own startup errors still do not meet that boundary contract.

### High — Required acceptance evidence remains missing

No tests were added for the exported Effect workflow. Deterministic `TestClock` pacing/exhaustion/interruption, spawn-failure marker release/no retry, 20-way singleton convergence, a true bind race, and incompatibility before/after acquisition and while waiting remain unproved.

